#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
yokto ai-menu
=============
Menu + CLI for the --ai image: model management (download/list/remove),
llama-server control (start/stop/status) and chat launchers
(langchain chat or plain llama-cli chat).

The model catalogue is memory-aware: the Pi 5 ships with 4 GB or 8 GB RAM,
and llama.cpp is CPU-only here, so the menu ranks models by what fits and
runs smoothly on the detected RAM.

CLI / programmable use (no human interaction needed):

  ai-menu --list                          # catalogue + installed status + RAM tier
  ai-menu --ram                           # print detected RAM / recommended tier
  ai-menu --download qwen0.5              # download a model (by id or name fragment)
  ai-menu --download --id 2 --force       # download by catalogue number, re-fetch
  ai-menu --remove llama3.2-1b            # delete a downloaded model file
  ai-menu --server start --model 2        # start llama-server with catalogue id 2
  ai-menu --server start --model /path/x.gguf
  ai-menu --server stop
  ai-menu --server status
  ai-menu --chat langchain --model 2 --prompt "hello" --json
  ai-menu --chat simple   --model 2 --prompt "hello"
  ai-menu --chat langchain --model 2      # interactive

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 not found.
"""

